================================================================================
Pattern detection performance (hub pruning, single-pass signatures, stage_ms)
================================================================================

Context:
Detect on large graphs was slow: hop joins exploded through hubs before the
frontier cap applied, types were re-joined every hop, signatures were
recomputed per detail level, and shapes scanned every member. This change
instruments stages, prunes hub expansion, denormalises types, hashes all
detail levels in one pass, and builds non-refined shapes from one
representative anchor — without changing pattern_id hashing.

Changes:

1. src/jobs/graph_analytics_job.py
   Per-stage timers (`stage_ms`); single-pass `_sigs` with collect_set;
   `_dir` carries src_type/dst_type; `_reps` for shapes; narrowed refine
   top-N; `--pattern-hub-degree` (default 5000) skips walking through hubs.
2. resources/pattern_detection.job.yml
   New job parameter `pattern_hub_degree`.
3. src/back/core/graph_analysis/pattern/JobPatterns.py
   Passes `pattern_hub_degree`; summary surfaces hub_degree / hub_count.
4. tests/units/core/test_graph_analytics_job_sql.py
   SQLite `collect_set` shim.
5. tests/units/core/test_pattern_job_sql.py
   Instrumentation, single-pass, denorm, rep-shape, and hub-pruning tests.
6. tests/units/core/test_job_patterns.py
   Asserts hub-degree job parameter.
7. docs/architecture.md / docs/user-guide.md
   Hub pruning and stage_ms notes.
8. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-16-pattern-detection-performance-design.md
   Spec marked implemented.
9. docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-16-pattern-detection-performance.md
   Implementation plan.

