## Community and Pattern run history in Settings → Automation → Runs

Context:
Community detection and Pattern detection wrote no run history, so an
admin could not see past Detect runs, their status, or their failures
(Analytics, Build and Simulation already had one). Two new tabs on
Settings → Automation → Runs list Detect runs across every domain. Scope
was confirmed as those two tabs only (no Intelligence-page tabs). Storage
is two new Lakebase tables. Events are Detect only, completed and failed
rows, same as Analytics. Design: `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-16-analysis-run-history-design.md`.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/schema.sql
   New `community_runs` and `pattern_runs` tables with
   `(domain_id, version, computed_at DESC)` indexes, same shape and cap as
   `graph_analytics_runs`.
2. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/DetectRuns.py (new)
   Mixin for both tables driven by one `_KINDS` spec: lazy create
   (information_schema check, fail-soft), record (best-effort, per-
   `(domain, version)` cap of 100), cross-domain paged read with total.
3. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/store.py
   Mixes in `DetectRuns`; per-kind lazy-create flags; both tables added to
   `_KNOWN_TABLES`.
4. src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/__init__.py
   Exports `DetectRuns`.
5. src/back/objects/registry/store/base.py
   `CommunityRun` / `PatternRun` documented aliases (the architecture ratchet
   caps the number of classes per file); no-op / `([], 0)` defaults for the
   four store methods.
6. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/DetectRunHistory.py (new)
   `DetectRunHistory.record_community` / `record_pattern`: build the row from
   the job summary (or the error) and append it through `svc.store`. Best-effort,
   never changes the task outcome. Extracted from `TwinBackgroundTasks` to keep
   it inside the 800-LOC class budget.
7. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/TwinBackgroundTasks.py
   `run_community_task` and `run_pattern_task` record one row on completion and
   one on failure.
8. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/__init__.py
   Re-exports `DetectRunHistory`.
9. src/back/objects/domain/settings/ScheduleSettings.py
   `_all_runs_result` accepts kinds `community` and `pattern`.
10. src/api/routers/internal/settings.py
   `GET /settings/runs/community` and `GET /settings/runs/patterns`
   (domain / limit / offset, same envelope as the other run readers).
11. src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_runs.html
   Two new tabs (Community runs, Pattern runs) with their own loading / empty
   / error / table / pagination elements, between Analytics and Simulation.
12. src/front/templates/settings.html
   Two page-level details modals (`srCommunityRunDetailsModal`,
   `srPatternRunDetailsModal`).
13. src/front/static/config/js/settings-runs.js
   Two descriptors in `TABS`, state, paging reset, load order, detail
   builders and window handlers for both tabs.
14. src/front/static/global/js/runs-render.js
   `communityRunCells`, `communityRunDetailsHtml`, `patternRunCells`,
   `patternRunDetailsHtml`, plus a job-run link helper.
15. tests/units/registry/_v090_fake_pg.py
   Registers the two new lazy-create flags with the scripted harness.
16. tests/units/registry/test_v090_lakebase_detect_runs.py (new)
   Lazy create, record binds and cap, no-op without table, cross-domain paging,
   mapping and fail-soft reads for both tables.
17. tests/units/dtwin/test_v090_detect_run_history.py (new)
   Completed and failed rows for both tasks, failing write does not change the
   outcome, missing scope skips the write, Save/Materialize write nothing.
18. tests/units/settings/test_all_runs_endpoints.py
   Community and pattern routes join the paging / domain-filter / not-configured
   matrix.
19. tests/units/front/test_settings_runs_page.py
   Tab, pane, state-element, pagination, modal and script contracts for the two
   new tabs.
20. docs/user-guide.md, docs/api.md, docs/architecture.md
   Runs tab description, the two endpoints, and the two new tables.
21. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-16-analysis-run-history-design.md (new, gitignored)
   Design record for this change.

Decisions:
- Lakebase is the only registry backend, so the tables live there; the base
  store defaults are no-ops for any other backend.
- Existing deployments get the tables lazily on first write or read; fresh
  deployments get them from `schema.sql`.

